  "published": "2026-09-28T08:50:59.253Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.1: adds the jsmn copyright and permission notice (THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt) to the package; no code change. 2.0.0: the request pipeline is built around UTF-8 bytes (ReadOnlySequence, ReadOnlyMemory or ReadOnlySpan in, IBufferWriter out), the JSON serializer is pluggable with the built-in serializer as the default and Json.NET and System.Text.Json as packages, and Task and ValueTask methods are supported again through ProcessAsync with cooperative cancellation. Document and batch limits are on by default (JsonRpcLimits), reserved method names are refused at registration, unknown named parameters are rejected, an error handler receives the exception the method threw, and the four assemblies are strong-named with one key that stays fixed from here on. Six times the throughput of 1.2.3 through the 1.x string API and twenty-four times through the byte entry points, measured on a 32-core Hugging Face Jobs host (see the README). InProcessClient is removed; three legacy members are obsolete at warning level with diagnostic ids JSONRPC0001 to JSONRPC0003. What is new: https://astn.github.io/JSON-RPC.NET/changelog.html. Upgrading from 1.x: https://astn.github.io/JSON-RPC.NET/upgrading.html",
